v2.0.0 - 2026/11/04

 - Fork maintained at https://github.com/matteosecli/ocproxy

 - Merge upstream PRs #14, #18, #21, #30 (HTTP proxy, -H), #33 (backpressure
   instead of dropping packets on socketpair overflow)

 - Update bundled lwIP to 2.2.1 (NO_SYS raw API, no pthreads); remove the
   -T/--tcpdump option (no longer provided by lwIP)

 - Default to a 64 MiB lwIP heap and 256 KiB TCP send buffer / receive window
   (window scaling, shift 3); tunable via -DOCPROXY_* at configure time

 - Scale lwIP TCP segment and packet-buffer pool targets with the TCP buffer
   sizes and heap budget

 - Add end-to-end test suite ("make check") and GitHub Actions CI/release

 - Provide static musl (Alpine) binaries; fix build on musl libc

 - Have the vpnns watcher process re-create the bind mount if the underlying
   resolv.conf is deleted (e.g. by NetworkManager)

 - Eliminate the possible 1-second delay when starting a new vpnns instance

 - Minor manpage update

v1.60 - 2017/01/08

 - Allow specifying the local SOCKS address via "-D <addr>:<port>".

 - Add experimental vpnns program

v1.50 - 2014/07/06

 - Fix a bunch of stability issues seen under load (web browsing on SOCKS)

 - Add man page

 - Switch build system to GNU autotools

 - Update to the latest lwIP and fix DNS lookup bugs

 - Delete unused netmask and gateway options

 - Add scripts to build one-off packages for Ubuntu PPA

 - Use Travis CI to run automated builds on each commit

v1.20121120160713 - 2012/11/20

 - Initial release.
